        "original_id": "3a6384e8-ac8b-5d56-ac59-8f2140694a3d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Tom Araya, Marcus Mumford\n- Organizations: Slayer, Mumford & Sons, Grammy Awards\n- Products: \"Eyes of the Insane\", \"30/30-150\"\n\nFacts:\n- Tom Araya was born on June 6, 1961, and he is a Chilean American musician.\n- Tom Araya is best known as the vocalist and bassist of the American thrash metal band Slayer.\n- Marcus Mumford was born on January 31, 1987, and he is a British-American singer, songwriter, musician, and producer.\n- Marcus Mumford is best known as the lead singer of the band Mumford & Sons.\n- Tom Araya wrote the song \"Eyes of the Insane\" during pre-production for its album.\n- At the 49th Annual Grammy Awards, the song \"30/30-150\" was nominated for Best Metal Performance.\n- At the 49th Annual Grammy Awards, \"30/30-150\" lost Best Metal Performance to Slayer's \"Eyes of the Insane\".",
